                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is a port of the 3DS remake of Steel Empire. It is a no-frills port without any extra settings to customize it for the PC beyond what was presented in the original 3DS version. It is not a remaster or \"HD remake\" and is exactly the same game as Steel Empire on the 3DS.\n\nIt has a number of issues on modern systems despite coming out in 2018:\n\n1. The game is capped at 30 FPS and struggles to reach that. It drops frames frequently to compensate. While this doesn't slow down the game play or affect playability, dropped frames make it harder to react and track enemy bullets during fast action sequences.\n\n2. The audio mixing is very strange, the player shot effects are extremely loud and the remaining effects and music are not as loud. When there's more effects playing the overall volume of the mixed audio gets lower. You can lower the effects balance in the option menu but it still sounds odd.\n\n3. If your PC has a DPI setting that isn't 100% the game window is scaled larger than your screen. You have to use the compatibility settings on the game executable to force 100% DPI to make the game work.\n\n4. Nearly all graphics have blurry edges which is a shame for a game with such excellent pixel art. Furthermore many elements have a 1 pixel gray border around everything.  This is some kind of artefact from how the objects are composited is not how the original game looked. It's definitely a bug.\n\nOverall the game feels like something that was handed off to a very inexperienced team to manage the PC port.\n\nSteel Empire is a great game and really embodies the best elements of shoot-em-ups before that genre became \"bullet hell\" games and the original style ceased to exist. That said, it's hard to recommend this port.  If you can, play it on the 3DS or even the original game on the Genesis. \n\nI got this game on sale for $1.49 and that felt like a rip-off given all the performance, audio, and video issues. It is absolutely not worth the non-sale price of $14.99.",
